<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dantewada</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Dantewara</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dantewada is a town in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhattisgarh">Chhattisgarh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, the headquarters of Dantewada district, at the confluence of the Shankhini and Dankini rivers. It is named after the goddess <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danteshwari">Danteshwari</a>, whose temple there was the shrine of the Rajas of Bastar. The surrounding forested district has large iron-ore mines at Bailadila.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dantewada.jpg" alt="Dantewada" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: PUNAM CHAND YADAV · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mai_ji_mandir_dantewada.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
